tools.description:
Puts the user's AI BLOGGER into a source clip (the quick form of the Miracle tab - for several people, styles or added people use miracle_analyze + miracle), in one of three modes:
'motion' (default; motion transfer) - the blogger performs the movement of the clip;
'recast' - the blogger replaces the person IN the clip, keeping its scene, camera, light and sound;
'swap' - an outfit, product, location or on-screen text in the clip is replaced from 1-4 photos; no blogger needed (same as swap_object).
ENGINE: 'seedance' (DEFAULT - Seedance 2.5, the whole 4-30 s clip in ONE pass, its scene and cuts kept, 720p, 10 credits per second; needs a saved bloggerId - a draft goes on Kling; when Seedance cannot take the clip the run goes on Kling by itself) or 'kling' (Kling 3.0, 1080p, about 6 credits per second: motion is Motion Control in the blogger's OWN framing and background with framing 'full' | 'half'; recast and swap 3-10 s). Optional lineText makes the blogger SAY a line in their pinned voice, lip-synced, replacing the clip's sound (motion on both engines, recast on seedance). Source: exactly one of presetId (list_blogger_presets), sourceGenerationId (the user's clip) or libraryItemId (create_upload kind 'video'). The performer must show a complete upper body (refused with motion_no_body otherwise - the credits come back automatically). SPENDS CREDITS per second of the source plus speech and lipsync per second for a line. Quote the exact price first - estimate_cost kind 'blogger_motion' (sourceSeconds, chars of the line, model = the engine), 'recast' or 'swap' - and get a yes. Returns a generation_id; call wait_for_generation.
